Proposed, NOT applied: the c4 format row + a 4mm-margin AltaLink row.
Generated 2026-08-18 against dec3cb5. Apply with `git apply <this file>`.

Two independent changes — split them if only one is wanted:

1. FORMAT AXIS — the c4-r0550 row (format/layout.py, format/descriptor.py,
   format/registry.py, receive/discovery_state.py, tests, HOLO-DESIGN §4.1).
   c4 = 4 dots/cell at 600 dpi = the c2 cell of a 300 dpi grid; the
   robustness rung below c3, 26x18 = 468 tiles on A4. The tile stays 64x64
   cells, so every layer above the raster is bit-identical in construction
   to c2/c3 — only the solid-cell dot expansion changes. Every edit either
   widens an accept-set or appends a row: no existing row's bits move, no
   golden edited, DEFAULT_DISCOVERY_ROW_IDS unchanged (cold-start discovery
   still trials exactly c3-r0550/c2-r0550/c2-r0700, same null budget), so
   decode needs an explicit --coding c4-r0550.
   Verified 2026-08-18, simulation only: cell-domain round trip byte-exact
   with 30% of tiles dropped (golden-pinned test_c4_r0550_roundtrip_byte_exact);
   blind pixel-domain receiver run on a synthetic 7x7-tile c4 page,
   byte-exact; blind run on a full emitted A4 c4 page's ground truth,
   32,622 B byte-exact. Suite 1229 passed / 42 skipped.
   UNQUALIFIED ON PAPER: no c4 sheet has ever been printed.

2. DEVICE DATA — xerox-altalink-c8245-ink (devices/registry.py), a 4.0mm
   geometry probe mirroring hp-m281-ink. Capability data, no code path.
   Only c2 gains from it (1872 -> 1961 tiles, borders ~4.91/4.74mm); the
   c3 and c4 fields are quantization-identical at 4.0 and 6.0mm. The
   AltaLink's printable clip has never been measured the way e028 measured
   the M281 — 007.6 only says ticks survive to 4mm.

The sheets in scratch/xerox-v1-20260818/ were generated with this applied;
the c4 sheet (A) cannot be regenerated or decoded without it.

